This repository is a throughline *source*: a requirements graph, not a program. It
re-expresses the Linux kernel coding style as a grounded IDD graph so consuming
projects can compose it with throughline-compose.

The Linux kernel coding style is part of the Linux kernel documentation, published by
the Linux kernel developers at kernel.org under the GPL-2.0 licence. The rule text
re-expressed here in items' `text`/`attrs.source_ref` is derived from that guide and
remains the work of the Linux kernel developers and its contributors; this repository
claims no ownership over that content and reproduces it for interoperability. See
https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/process/coding-style.html for the authoritative
source.
